+
+The new sequential coordinator wraps the existing conversion workflow; it does
+not replace or duplicate it. Select one operation from the accepted plan, provide
+its resolved dependency contracts, invoke the current workflow through completion,
+publish its service record/checkpoint, then advance. Keep existing conversion,
+generation, assembly, packaging, test, review and bounded-correction behavior;
+adapt only the entry points needed to run that workflow for the current operation.
+
+Apply the existing four gates per operation with their current configurable
+human/automatic/skip policies. Gate One carries plan approval and the operation's
+scope, rather than adding a fifth job-approval gate. Gate evidence identifies the
+operation as well as the gate. All-human settings can require four approvals per
+operation; users may disable individual human pauses using the existing settings.
+Failed technical checks or dependency blockers still stop conversion, regardless
+of gate policy. Pause the coordinator at a pending/rejected gate and retain its
+current operation for Resume. Gate placement is settled by this reuse rule, not
+an open requirement for another approval mechanism.
 
